# Hand-written xcheck v1 topology: RK3588 (VOP2), NanoPC-T6 recording.
#
# Source file : tests/data/rk3588/topology-2026-11-28.md (observed 2026-11-28, kernel
#               6.18.55 recording, topology session only, no frame submitted)
# Commit      : eab4162 (HEAD when this file was written)
# Observed    : 2026-11-28
# Constraints : read from docs/rk3588-backend-design.md (design note of
#               2026-11-28); only limits that note states are written below.
# This file gives no hardware claim. It is a recorded description plus
# limits quoted from a design note; no frame was ever run on it.
#
# Truncation: the probe prints at most 32 formats per plane (design
# libliftoff-crosscheck.md section 3). The Cluster planes (33, 39, 45, 51)
# have more than 32 (format, modifier) pairs; their lists below end inside
# the AFBC 0x800000000000011 group exactly as in the dump, so the planes
# here accept fewer pairs than the real ones. Esmart lists are complete (21).
#
# zpos_now: the reset order recorded in the dump (normalized-zpos = plane
# index 0..7, Cluster0 0 ... Esmart3 7; rk3588-backend-design.md section 5
# and the dump's Planes section).
#
# Not documented, so written as the 'none' value (no invented limit):
#   full_output=0 on every plane, no 'group' line (design section 4 says no
#   scaler group is needed; a layer-budget group of capacity 8 is left out
#   until the budget is observed, Q4), transforms=- (the dump did not read
#   the rotation bitmask; the design's rotation table depends on the
#   buffer modifier and has no per-plane form), Cluster1 outputs=0x0 as the
#   probe printed it (only the connected output is modelled).
xcheck 1
origin observed 2026-11-28 rk3588-topology.md at commit eab4162; constraints read from rk3588-backend-design.md
profile generic

# observed 2026-11-28: video_port0, crtc 81, 1920x1080 @ 60.000 Hz
output 81 1920 1080 60000

# Cluster0-win0, reset zpos 0
# scaling: rk3588-backend-design.md section 4 table, Cluster column (read from source:
#   Cluster hardware 4x; the kernel check lets 1/8..8 through, the tighter
#   Cluster figure is the safe choice, inferred). 4x = 0x40000 in 16.16.
# max_source: rk3588-backend-design.md section 4 table, max_source row (read from source:
#   4096x7680; splice doubles the width only for hdisplay > 4096, not modelled).
